    - target: {fileID: 3620617087746342366, guid: 349f2c1b94a0b9341a4c306e7ac0c756, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Van de Wetering, considered one of the world\u2019s foremost Rembrandt
        experts until his death in 2021, often discussed Rembrandt\u2019s habit of
        \"witnessing\" his own scenes. He noted that Rembrandt frequently included
        himself in historical or group paintings (known as pittore nel quadro) to
        act as a narrator or a signature.\nGiven Rembrandt's playful attitude, the
        figure's hat, nose and side glance the theory this might be Rembrandt himself
        gained a lot of followers in the research community. "
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
