    - target: {fileID: 3620617087746342366, guid: 349f2c1b94a0b9341a4c306e7ac0c756, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Jan Aertszn van der Heede (Driebruggen, 1610 \u2013 buried Amsterdam,
        May 11, 1655), son of Aert Huigenszn and Margaretha Amelsdr van der Heede,
        was a musketeer in the Amsterdam civic guard of District II.\nVan der Heede
        is depicted while loading his musket. He was identified in the painting in
        2009 by the Dutch historian Bas Dudok van Heel. \nProfessionally, he was
        a dealer in grocery goods."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
